.TH UNLZ4 1
.SH NAME
unlz4 \- decompress the LZ4 frame format
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B unlz4
[ infile [ outfile ] ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I unlz4
reads an LZ4 frame and writes the original bytes.  With no arguments,
or with
.B -
as a name, the standard input and output are used.
.PP
It accepts frames carrying a content size and block or content
checksums, skipping them; the header checksum is read but not verified.
The history window is 16383 bytes, matching
.IR lz4 (1),
so offsets beyond that are rejected.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
lz4(1), tar(1)
